{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality","id":1046066,"title":"Immortality","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-08T16:50:32-08:00","id":1046066,"title":"Immortality","content":"One of the formulas listed as an example for the fourth level of Alchemy in Sorcerer: Revised is a potion of longevity. Success seems to produce a year's worth of the regime of drugs that slows the aging process to one month for every year that they take the regime of drugs (they age one month every day that they lose access to their drugs until they reach their true age). A character who started the regime at age 25 would be physically 50 when they reached the age of 325 (they would be physically 75 when they reached the age of 625 and physically 100 when they reached the age of 925). With that type of longevity available from the efforts of Sorcerers, why would any Mage bother with using True Magick to retard aging, especially since it causes Pattern Bleed and Permanent Paradox after the first century or so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:57:29-08:00","id":1046072,"title":"","content":"Because it does neither of those if you do it right. Aka using it as an excuse to grab the unaging merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T17:08:05-08:00","id":1046075,"title":"","content":"Does the Unaging Merit specifically say that Mages who possess it are immune to Pattern Bleed or Permanent Paradox caused by True Magick longevity treatments? If so, can you give a book and page number please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T17:14:07-08:00","id":1046077,"title":"","content":"It just says &quot;you don't age.&quot; And leaves it up to you to explain why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T18:45:07-08:00","id":1046111,"title":"","content":"Then it does not provide immunity to Pattern Bleed or Permanent Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T18:49:35-08:00","id":1046113,"title":"","content":"I suspect it being a Merit means that, for whatever reason particular to the character's timelessness, it doesn't incur Paradox. If it did, the merit would have said so. This doesn't just apply to characters who achieved Unaging status by their own Art, but also those who achieved it through a wide variety of potential methods. Eating peaches of immortality, receiving a boon (or curse) from a higher (or lower) power, being injected with experimental nanomachines, a particularly potent Time-based Paradox backlash (or more probably a Scourge backlash, from the time when such things weren't always detrimental to the Mage), etc.<br /> <br /> Naturally, it would behoove a Storyteller to make the merit a burden in ways other than Paradox. People tend to pay attention (and react badly) to those who seem not to age over decades of time. Some of these people are specifically looking for (and align themselves against) those who display such unnatural traits. The Technocratic Union is only one such organization, though one of the most potent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T19:07:02-08:00","id":1046121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046111#post1046111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then it does not provide immunity to Pattern Bleed or Permanent Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't cause them either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T19:07:12-08:00","id":1046122,"title":"","content":"No, considering how many editions of the Mage game existed before Revised, I think it would be hard to say that they forgot to mention immunity to Paradox or Pattern Bleed. Unaging is not created through True Magick, it is either from a higher power or from an accident that could not be replicated (I am unaware of any rote that gives characters Supernatural Merits). Replicating Unaging with True Magick would still cause Paradox and Pattern Bleed because you would only be using a Life or Time effect to stop aging (and you would suffer a difficulty modifier to all effect rolls because you would be maintaining an ongoing effect, even if you make it permanent it is still on ongoing effect). If you want permanent augmentations without a difficulty modifier, get a Device or a Talisman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T19:18:47-08:00","id":1046125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046122#post1046122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, considering how many editions of the Mage game existed before Revised, I think it would be hard to say that they forgot to mention immunity to Paradox or Pattern Bleed. Unaging is not created through True Magick, it is either from a higher power or from an accident that could not be replicated (I am unaware of any rote that gives characters Supernatural Merits). Replicating Unaging with True Magick would still cause Paradox and Pattern Bleed because you would only be using a Life or Time effect to stop aging (and you would suffer a difficulty modifier to all effect rolls because you would be maintaining an ongoing effect, even if you make it permanent it is still on ongoing effect). If you want permanent augmentations without a difficulty modifier, get a Device or a Talisman.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you don't maintain it if it has a duration for one. That's like saying you're pushing a car when it has an engine that pushes the car and you along with it.<br /> <br /> For two, it doesn't mention that because it takes a very convoluted reading of the merit to try and say that you should have permanent paradox and pattern bleeding because of it.<br /> <br /> For three, Life Five, Perfect Metamorphosis. You do whatever you feel like with your pattern and laugh off pattern bleeding because you decide what your pattern is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T20:46:17-08:00","id":1046159,"title":"","content":"Ongoing effects give difficulty penalties (Mage: Revised, p. 155-156). If you have a specific book and page number that states that duration negates the ongoing effects penalty, please feel free to share. Otherwise, the only way I know to avoid ongoing effects modifiers is by making Devices or Talismans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-08-2017, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T05:58:06-08:00","id":1046271,"title":"","content":"Use Alchemy 6, you can become a Revenant and Quarter the rate again forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T05:59:58-08:00","id":1046272,"title":"","content":"Probably for a few reasons.<br /> -Requires a strong mastery of Alchemy, which, when you already have a real form of enlightenment, probably seems unimportant in comparison.<br /> -Still presents risks as far as not having your potion when you need it.<br /> -Could die outright for a botch preparing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T06:24:25-08:00","id":1046279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046272#post1046272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably for a few reasons.<br /> -Requires a strong mastery of Alchemy, which, when you already have a real form of enlightenment, probably seems unimportant in comparison.<br /> -Still presents risks as far as not having your potion when you need it.<br /> -Could die outright for a botch preparing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus the ST doesn't have to let Mages have Sorcery. I'm sure there are plenty of Mages (even Archmages) who wish they could whip up a Storm or conjure fire without paradox (ESPECIALLY since they could follow up with some paradox-free Magick, for example manipulating an existing fire is far less vulgar then creating one out of nowhere and is easier to pass as consensual), but they can't. The Avatar won't play ball, it's woken up and it won't let you play around with Reality when you could be rewriting Reality.<br /> <br /> Well... sort of? 1 EXP lowers the difficulty by 1 forever. After that, you just spend Mana each time you do it. Recovering Mana can be as simple as waiting, meditating or having sex. And most Sorcerer PCs will have Mana. The likelihood of you botching a difficulty 5 roll is quite low, especially if you spend Willpower on it (it's only once a month) and learn the skills related to &quot;casting&quot; it up to their highest level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T06:24:43-08:00","id":1046280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046271#post1046271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Use Alchemy 6, you can become a Revenant and Quarter the rate again forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting idea, though you could potentially become practically anything with Alchemy 6 (except for a Changeling, Demon, or Wraith).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T06:33:56-08:00","id":1046282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably for a few reasons.<br /> -Still presents risks as far as not having your potion when you need it.<br /> -Could die outright for a botch preparing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have problams with this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Requires a strong mastery of Alchemy, which, when you already have a real form of enlightenment, probably seems unimportant in comparison. </div> </div> </div>Hubris it's always good, but it shouldn't be excuse for stupidity or lack of knowledge. When you go so far as to become vampire or make a deal with the devil for immortailty, the rumor that some static mages live really long lives should have reached the ears of at least a few archmasters, and they shouldn't be above of manipulating them to get the potion. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Could die outright for a botch preparing it. </div> </div> </div>High Ritual magick to make you immortal can be quite deadly too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Still presents risks as far as not having your potion when you need it. </div> </div> </div>This, however, it's more like it. But it's a bit silly to exile yourself from Earth because a fear off forgetting the longevity potion. Just use Mind to ensure you don't forget it. Now, if you were going to leave Earth anyway...<br /> <br /> I think that Sorcerer: Revised disregards some of the most basic assumptions of Mage. It shouldn't be so easy to get longevity, becasue longevity was a forbbiden fruit in Mage from the day 1. It was that, more than anything else, what forced Master into the Umbra (as Realms avoid the gain of Permadox until you get back to Earth, Pattern Bleeding wasn't a thing back then, but I would assume that Realms would counter that too, to keep the story intact). It was the reason why Tremere turned vampire. If a static mage can grant you that, or something close to that, immortality looses it's &quot;forbbiden fruit&quot; appeal (and mages seem like morons for not using that solution). A similar thing happens with Ghouldoom without extra consequences, but being a blood adict with awfull resonance it's a better reason not to search this kind of immortality than thinking that &quot;static magick it's unimportant, if isn't dynamic, I don't do it&quot;. Now, if there were consequences from taking the static solution, like being filled with statism, and loosing some hability with dynamic magick, then it would make more sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-09-2017, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T06:54:06-08:00","id":1046293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046279#post1046279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Plus the ST doesn't have to let Mages have Sorcery. I'm sure there are plenty of Mages (even Archmages) who wish they could whip up a Storm or conjure fire without paradox (ESPECIALLY since they could follow up with some paradox-free Magick, for example manipulating an existing fire is far less vulgar then creating one out of nowhere and is easier to pass as consensual), but they can't. The Avatar won't play ball, it's woken up and it won't let you play around with Reality when you could be rewriting Reality.<br /> <br /> Well... sort of? 1 EXP lowers the difficulty by 1 forever. After that, you just spend Mana each time you do it. Recovering Mana can be as simple as waiting, meditating or having sex. And most Sorcerer PCs will have Mana. The likelihood of you botching a difficulty 5 roll is quite low, especially if you spend Willpower on it (it's only once a month) and learn the skills related to &quot;casting&quot; it up to their highest level.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair idea. But anyway, the chance of botching increases exponentially when the example ages were 325, 625, and 925. If you've lived that long, you're already making the check 3,900, 7500, and 11,100 times respectively? Plus, I think you have to put three or four days into preparing it for most, unless I'm looking at that wrong, but seems like a fair time sink. As well as burning a will each time you prepare it. Two if you really want to be safe/sure, in which case you are pretty focused on making sure you keep that will up. Though, idk Revised super well, so some of this might be off. Not necessarily always able to reduce that 8 difficulty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046282#post1046282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hubris it's always good, but it shouldn't be excuse for stupidity or lack of knowledge. When you go so far as to become vampire or make a deal with the devil for immortailty, the rumor that some static mages live really long lives should have reached the ears of at least a few archmasters, and they shouldn't be above of manipulating them to get the potion.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't know, I feel like forcing a sorcerer to make you and himself this potion every month only increases the risk. I'm not trying to imply that it isn't an alright shot at immortality. Just that it falls short of true immortality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> High Ritual magick to make you immortal can be quite deadly too. </div> </div> </div> Agreed. But learning high level magic is inherently going to be in the program of a mage to try and learn. Whereas he's going out of his way to learn a different form of potentially risky lesser magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This, however, it's more like it. But it's a bit silly to exile yourself from Earth because a fear off forgetting the longevity potion. Just use Mind to ensure you don't forget it. Now, if you were going to leave Earth anyway... </div> </div> </div>Well, it wasn't necessarily about forgetting to take it. I'd say this part would have to be something that is very ST specific. As in, what is actually needed for a character to make this potion. And what circumstances might make you unable to. But the risk is there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that Sorcerer: Revised disregards some of the most basic assumptions of Mage. It shouldn't be so easy to get longevity, becasue longevity was a forbbiden fruit in Mage from the day 1. It was that, more than anything else, what forced Master into the Umbra (as Realms avoid the gain of Permadox until you get back to Earth, Pattern Bleeding wasn't a thing back then, but I would assume that Realms would counter that too, to keep the story intact). It was the reason why Tremere turned vampire. If a static mage can grant you that, or something close to that, immortality looses it's &quot;forbbiden fruit&quot; appeal (and mages seem like morons for not using that solution). A similar thing happens with Ghouldoom without extra consequences, but being a blood adict with awfull resonance it's a better reason not to search this kind of immortality than thinking that &quot;static magick it's unimportant, if isn't dynamic, I don't do it&quot;. Now, if there were consequences from taking the static solution, like being filled with statism, and loosing some hability with dynamic magick, then it would make more sense </div> </div> </div>I really didn't just want to say, 'because it is poorly written.' But yeah, immorality as a thing for Mages is a fairly idealized goal in the setting. As far as Mummies and Tremere, etc as failings. So the math behind this power isn't great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","user":"Monalfie","date":". 02-09-2017, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T07:13:00-08:00","id":1046300,"title":"","content":"Why does everyone think that the Alchemy 4 formula only makes enough for one month? From my reading, it is a year's worth of longevity drug that slows your aging to one month per year, but you have to take the regime every day to avoid aging (you age one month per day of missing the regime, not per day after you have missed a monthly dose). I can see Mages desiring other longevity solutions because 1) they do not want to depend on magic they cannot control to give them longevity, 2) it is longevity and they desire true immortality, and 3) it is annoying to take a drug every day when they want an effortless solution.<br /> <br /> Tremere converted to vampirism because the methods to grant himself eternal youth were falling, not necessarily because there was not alternative that could have given him longevity. When he realized he could look forward to centuries of slow decline due to aging, I think that he decided to attempt to avoid aging by researching vampirism. He succeeded and, by trading the change that came from aging for the stasis of immortality, he traded the dynamic magic of Mages for the linear magic of Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T07:39:25-08:00","id":1046309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046300#post1046300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does everyone think that the Alchemy 4 formula only makes enough for one month? From my reading, it is a year's worth of longevity drug that slows your aging to one month per year, but you have to take the regime every day to avoid aging (you age one month per day of missing the regime, not per day after you have missed a monthly dose). I can see Mages desiring other longevity solutions because 1) they do not want to depend on magic they cannot control to give them longevity, 2) it is longevity and they desire true immortality, and 3) it is annoying to take a drug every day when they want an effortless solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it is unclear and that seemed like the most logic reading to me since I'm used to ghouls.<br /> The duration is listed as 'Varies, but normally one scene.'<br /> &quot;A regimen of drugs and potions that extends the user's life (though not indefinitely). While on the regimen, the user ages at the rate of one month for every year. If the regimen is halted, these years come back upon the user at the rate of one month per day, until the regimen is started back up or the user dies of old age.&quot;<br /> It doesn't give details on how much of this regimen is made when it is cast. Or how often you have to take the regimen. So my default was 'makes enough for one month, lasts one month, taken once a month.' But seemingly it could be read in a few different ways. I think your reading is equally valid, but it isn't clear cut either way, unless I'm not looking at the language right. All it says is that once the regimen is halted, this regimen having no defined quantity/period, you start again each day.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T07:40:53-08:00","id":1046311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046280#post1046280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting idea, though you could potentially become practically anything with Alchemy 6 (except for a Changeling, Demon, or Wraith).</div> </div> </div> </div>Revenant is, in my opinion, the best option. A random human who becomes a Revenant halfway through life is a very happy person, having had a normal aging and upbringing up to that point. The Frenzy risk is minimal, and you get a tonne of benefits with very few weaknesses. Plus if you take the 'Blood Sorcery' Merit you've just gained 10 points of Spell-Casting power for your Sorcery... along with soak of Lethal. Plus for every 100 years as a Revenant, your blood pool grows by 1. Furthermore, really old Revenants take bashing damage from bullets, so when guns come around they'll be a funny distraction.<br /> <br /> So someone with Alchemy 6 in the Dark Ages (at this point studying Revenants and extracting some alchemical factor from them would be fair) could quite easily quarter their aging, and then divide it by 12 for a total reduction of 48 times. Assuming they do this at Age 30, that gives them roughly 60 years left with perfect health and a perfect regime, which is something they're actively doing. 60 x 48 = 2440. So a Sorcerer could live for 2440 years, assuming no botches. That's 2440 rolls of about 15 dice against difficulty 3, with 3 mana spent and a perfect setting to make it in you would have a decent chance of never botching, especially if you spent 1+ Willpower too...<br /> <br /> The issue is things staying stable enough for 2400 years that you keep your lab and everything and have perfect conditions and the ingredients. At this point it's far easier to mix up something that forces a Vampire into Torpor, and keep them in Torpor in your basement for centuries, ghouling yourself off of it. Another level 6 ritual makes you unbondable, and you add restraints over the years in case they wake up. You'd refresh the Topor ritual every once in a while too, or just stake them. You force-feed them blood and then drain it back, reducing them to a piece of alchemical equipment.<br /> <br /> Combining the ritual effects of Mana Manipulation 6 and Alchemy 6 (you have PLENTY of time) you could increase your Blood Pool, Mana Pool, raise your Discipline limits... and you could carry an Alchemy 6 potion with you at all times that will embrace you if you drink it, just in case you're caught in a situation where you can't escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-09-2017, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T08:46:29-08:00","id":1046331,"title":"","content":"I do not think that you would have anyone surviving that long (probability of dying of accident or dusease eventually catches up), but it is a good origin story for an elder Kindred. What generation should the synthetic Kindred be? I was thinking 8th generation because Alchemy 6 is a rather steep requirement, with each success on the Alchemy test giving you an additional dose (the potion would only be stable for a week after creation). That way, you could potentially have a group of people (the master alchemist plus assistants) becoming Caitiff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T08:49:18-08:00","id":1046333,"title":"","content":"The only mention of Pattern Bleeding in M20 is this (p516)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When used to inflict or repair damage, Life deals out aggravated damage because it works directly upon the Patterns of living things. As a result, an organism that has been radically altered by Life magick (given new limbs or other characteristics that are not part of the creature\u2019s original Pattern) suffers Pattern bleeding: an inexorable Quintessence leak that inflicts one level of lethal damage per day. Unless the caster uses Prime magick to refill that Pattern with fresh energy, <b>or alters that Pattern permanently</b>, the damage continues until the subject dies. </div> </div> </div>Note my emphasis, it's possible to alter a pattern permanently so that it does not suffer pattern bleeding. Implying that the Unaging merit also causes one level of lethal damage per day would turn it from a 2 pt merit to a 5 pt flaw. Likewise insisting that Pattern Bleeding is inevitable and unavoidable with <i>any </i>immortality magic is also unreasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T10:06:38-08:00","id":1046365,"title":"","content":"That's one problem less. Thanks for that bit of information.<br /> <br /> You still have to contend with the Permadox, tough. In times of yore (of Horizon: Stronhold of Hope) you won 1 point of Permadox each 50 years after the first 150, unless you were living in a Horizon Realm. In Masters of the Art (other source of immortality rules) this isn't mentioned, moreso, it's said that some immortality magick can be Coincident, but if someone realizes you lived longer than any human, then you get a backlash with all the Paradox you should have gained. Does this mean that the old accruing of Permadox it's no longer a rule? Well, it was assumed for so long that Paradox forced immortal mages outside Earth that I don't see this as a good idea. There MUST be a dire reason for immortality to make mages go away, if we want to preserve that bit of lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-09-2017, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T10:14:10-08:00","id":1046368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046365#post1046365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one problem less.<br /> <br /> You still have to contend with the Permadox, tough. In times of yore (of Horizon: Stronhold of Hope) you won 1 point of Permadox each 50 years after the first 150, unless you were living in a Horizon Realm. In Masters of the Art (other source of immortality rules) this isn't mentioned, moreso, it's said that some immortality magick can be Coincident, but if someone realizes you lived longer than any human, then you get a backlash with all the Paradox you should have gained. Does this mean that the old accruing of Permadox it's no longer a rule? Well, it was assumed for so long that Paradox forced immortal mages outside Earth that I don't see this as a good idea. There MUST be a dire reason for immortality to make mages go away, if we want to preserve that bit of lore.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I think the threat that moves you away is permadox in general, not necessarily permadox from aging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","user":"Monalfie","date":". 02-09-2017, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T10:50:47-08:00","id":1046380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm pretty sure the given reason was that paradox backlash just becomes too severe for even relatively simple spells for those old archmages. </div> </div> </div>That's my understanding as well. This was a direct consequence of gaining Permanent Paradox. With allegedly &quot;paradox-free&quot; solutions, this becomes fuzzy. Of course, if the alternate solutions (like Sorcery), are deemed too risky (like you suggested), or have some other severe downside, the issue disappears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T11:20:22-08:00","id":1046388,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, Mages receive one point of permanent Paradox for every dot of Traits above '5' and for every permanent change to their patterns beyond normal human potential (every 50 years of age past 150 years being counted as one permanent change).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T11:47:27-08:00","id":1046396,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> RE Synthetic Kindred, I'd say it's down to their materials. So if you created the potion using the blood of three Vampires, you average their generations and drop by 1. So if you have three 12th Generation Kindred, it's 11th Generation. Three 8th Generation Vampires, 7th Generation. You could, if you want it dark, make it a Sacrifice, like the Skin Dancers who must absorb the pelts of three fallen Fera (who they must be Kinfolk to, so a Garou Kinfolk can skin three Garou and use that to become a Garou, however Spirits will see him and say &quot;nooooooooooooooooope&quot; whereas Banes will be VERY friendly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:00:50-08:00","id":1046402,"title":"","content":"Personally, one of the reasons I prefer the 20th anniversary editions is that they don't have that f*ck the players attitude that so many revised books seem to (Blood Treachery I'm looking at you, you skank). It feels like a lot of the pre 20th anniversary content beyond the core books is aimed at countering min-maxing or making it much harder to do something cool than in the base rules. I'm assuming it's a legacy of the times, a whole bunch of inexperienced storytellers, and that desperate need White Wolf had to 'publish anything' so as to stay afloat but it makes for a lot of rules that screw players over instead of expanding and enhancing their play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:08:37-08:00","id":1046409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046402#post1046402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, one of the reasons I prefer the 20th anniversary editions is that they don't have that f*ck the players attitude that so many revised books seem to (Blood Treachery I'm looking at you, you skank). It feels like a lot of the pre 20th anniversary content beyond the core books is aimed at countering min-maxing or making it much harder to do something cool than in the base rules. I'm assuming it's a legacy of the times, a whole bunch of inexperienced storytellers, and that desperate need White Wolf had to 'publish anything' so as to stay afloat but it makes for a lot of rules that screw players over instead of expanding and enhancing their play.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did Blood Treachery do that was so awful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:22:58-08:00","id":1046416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046409#post1046409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What did Blood Treachery do that was so awful?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having not read it myself, take this with a grain of salt. But in the core book it's possible to be a ghoul mage. You get the powers of a ghoul and a mage, and the usual downsides of being a ghoul. In addition it's hard to complete seekings, and you are loaded with entropic and static resonance.<br /> <br /> Blood treachery decided this was not emo enough, and had it so that over time being a ghoul mage not only halts the growth of your Arete, but lowers it. Slowly gilguling you in the process.<br /> <br /> Also I believe it contains another version of the rather broken countermagic rules where vampires get two dicepools rather than one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:37:10-08:00","id":1046423,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11744\" data-vbnamecard=\"11744\">Enginseer-42</a> People over-hype those. Yes, if you cast a freaking bolt of sunlight or fire at a Vampire they get a counter-magic roll (Wits + Occult), same with other Nightfolk. However, you could simply roll a level 1 effect and aim to hit them at -3 difficulty, or hit them with extra force, or make the floor beneath them go liquidy, or speed up your own time to take extra actions...<br /> <br /> Basically any assault which isn't Obviously Mystical is okay with Nightfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:47:22-08:00","id":1046429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046416#post1046416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood treachery decided this was not emo enough, and had it so that over time being a ghoul mage not only halts the growth of your Arete, but lowers it. Slowly gilguling you in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also says that a Revenant Mage would be Gilguled by his or her own Vitae; blood treachery, indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:51:47-08:00","id":1046432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046429#post1046429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also says that a Revenant Mage would be Gilguled by his or her own Vitae; blood treachery, indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you can't be a Mage full-stop if you're Kinfolk or a Revenant. They have a path set for them already, they come from a different world. They can be Sorcerers, but they don't have Avatars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:57:22-08:00","id":1046433,"title":"","content":"Blood Treachery was fine, it reduced the min-max potential of Ghoul Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:59:27-08:00","id":1046436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046433#post1046433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood Treachery was fine, it reduced the min-max potential of Ghoul Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and to be fair since a Ghoul Mage can simply use Mind to remove the blood bond, they can live forever Paradox free, soak Lethal damage, get a free dot of Potence to give those -3 difficulty blows an extra kick... plus the rapid healing and all of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:59:54-08:00","id":1046437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046432#post1046432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well you can't be a Mage full-stop if you're Kinfolk or a Revenant. They have a path set for them already, they come from a different world. They can be Sorcerers, but they don't have Avatars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wut. You most certainly can be a kinfolk mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:01:04-08:00","id":1046438,"title":"","content":"You can be Mages who are Kinfolk, but you cannot be Mages if you are Kinfolk who develop Gifts or Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:01:06-08:00","id":1046439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046437#post1046437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wut. You most certainly can be a kinfolk mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this one of those things where it happens both ways? Like I remember reading one thing which said basically &quot;NORMAL HUMANS ONLY&quot; and another which was more &quot;ST Discretion&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:02:26-08:00","id":1046440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046438#post1046438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can be Mages who are Kinfolk, but you cannot be Mages if you are Kinfolk who develop Gifts or Gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so we can say that if you exhibit zero hereditary supernatural traits, becoming a Mage is simple. So Changelings can't do it, for example, but someone with fae ancestry which didn't manifest mechanically (same with Fera ancestry or Ghoul ancestry) can become a Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:05:47-08:00","id":1046441,"title":"","content":"I see no particular problem with restricting Mages to humans only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:11:41-08:00","id":1046445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046441#post1046441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see no particular problem with restricting Mages to humans only.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, you use Life and Mind to make Lizard People who are as smart as humans. Can THEY become True Mages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:14:13-08:00","id":1046447,"title":"","content":"Nope, they do not have Avatars, so they cannot be Mages. Now, if you create an Avatar with Spirit 5, then you can make them True Mages, though they would suffer some seriously horrifying permanent Paradox because they are a walking violation of Reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:17:07-08:00","id":1046448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046447#post1046447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, they do not have Avatars, so they cannot be Mages. Now, if you create an Avatar with Spirit 5, then you can make them True Mages, though they would suffer some seriously horrifying permanent Paradox because they are a walking violation of Reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't Avatars just Angel Corpses from the First War which latch onto human spirits? Like even quite low Spirit could kind of nudge one on right, since it's just... spiritual detritus. Then again that's DTF lore, not Mage lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:17:48-08:00","id":1046449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046447#post1046447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, they do not have Avatars, so they cannot be Mages. Now, if you create an Avatar with Spirit 5, then you can make them True Mages, though they would suffer some seriously horrifying permanent Paradox because they are a walking violation of Reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Men in black are all made with life 5 but they are still mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T14:09:44-08:00","id":1046473,"title":"","content":"Actually, they are artifical constructs, so they lacked previous patterns that would prevent Awakening. Dealing with Avatars is very difficult for Mages (for example, forcing an Avatar to Awaken is a level 9 power).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-09-2017, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T17:19:12-08:00","id":1046537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046473#post1046473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, they are artifical constructs, so they lacked previous patterns that would prevent Awakening. Dealing with Avatars is very difficult for Mages (for example, forcing an Avatar to Awaken is a level 9 power).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my point. If you make a lizard man, that's just a human that looks like a lizard. While there's certainly every chance they'll be born soulless. There's also a chance they aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T18:15:11-08:00","id":1046565,"title":"","content":"Just to set the record straight, Mage Revised had Merits for playing Mages that were either Kinfolk (Shapechanger Kin, 4-Pt Merit), Kinian (Fae Blood, 4-Pt Merit), and Ghouls (Ghoul, 5-Pt Merit). So not only is it possible, there are mechanics covering them. Blood Treachery had a Merit for playing the descendant of gods, angels, demons, or other residents of the Astral Umbra (Nephilim, 7-Pt Merit).<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the Revised Storyteller's Handbook contains optional rules for Mages with any of those Merits, allowing them to draw upon the Mythic Threads that inherent to their being. If the Storyteller is willing, the character could cast Effects that emulate the powers of the relevant supernaturals, while being Coincidental. So long as those powers are attributed to them in popular consciousness, of course. (So, for instance, Celerity or Protean = Okay, Obtenebration or Vicissitude = Off Limits). Personally I find these rules more compelling than letting the characters buy powers from the other Splats. Everything is funneled through the Spheres, there's less book keeping, Experience isn't divided between two sets of systems, and Paradox is still a problem (if the character Botches).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T05:58:04-08:00","id":1046735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, the Revised Storyteller's Handbook contains optional rules for Mages with any of those Merits, allowing them to draw upon the Mythic Threads that inherent to their being. If the Storyteller is willing, the character could cast Effects that emulate the powers of the relevant supernaturals, while being Coincidental. So long as those powers are attributed to them in popular consciousness, of course. (So, for instance, Celerity or Protean = Okay, Obtenebration or Vicissitude = Off Limits). Personally I find these rules more compelling than letting the characters buy powers from the other Splats. Everything is funneled through the Spheres, there's less book keeping, Experience isn't divided between two sets of systems, and Paradox is still a problem (if the character Botches). </div> </div> </div>I like this thing. It plays with the concept of Mythic Threads instead of making them just an excuse to explain why supernaturals don't suffer Paradox. I like the M20 section, too, that mentions that if you use magick following the lines of a given Mythic Thread you gain advantages. The default advantage it's a -1 to difficulty (if you do magick that resembles &quot;clasic&quot; magick and fiction tropes), but the spell could also be considered Coincidental in special cases (like those mentioned above). It still may cause Paradox (in a botch), but being able to &quot;tap&quot; into the Threads to nullify or reduce the impact it's cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T01:55:32-08:00","id":1047612,"title":"","content":"&gt;Mythic Threads<br /> Yeah this is another reason why as far as I'm concerned M20 is far superior than the previous editions. Much less antagonistic to players much more a modern RPG than an eighties/nineties RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T19:32:53-08:00","id":1048036,"title":"","content":"Considering M20 seems just as antagonistic to the players, if not 100 times more so.... I don't get your point there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T03:08:44-08:00","id":1048148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1048036#post1048036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering M20 seems just as antagonistic to the players, if not 100 times more so.... I don't get your point there.</div> </div> </div> </div>100 times more antagonistic? I really don't get that.<br /> <br /> I mean, M20 has its pros and cons, yes. But aside of one, two points, I'd not call it really more antagonistic.<br /> <br /> * The system of Arete rolls has reverted to 1st/2nd/Sorc Crusade.<br /> As in, the *total* amount of successes determines the effect's parameters, instead of having to split up the dice between all of them (with the exception of Damage vs duration). The split successes rule is optional for those that want it, which is a plus.<br /> This especially allows younger Mages with smaller dice pools to achieve average effects with less rolls. No more repeated-orgies-of-ritual-rolls-for-small-things like in Revised. Thank deity-of-choice for that. Seriously.<br /> <br /> * Foci and tools-to-drop are not tied to spheres anymore.<br /> It never, ever made sense to me that you'd have to select a special focus for whole spheres, given that each level of a sphere can mean very different effects and VERY different practices of achieving them.<br /> Choose 'water' as a specialty focus for Time, because you figure '<i>hey, it's awesome flavor for my character to specialize in getting glimpses of past and future in the surfaces of ritual pools</i>' suddenly makes you require water in order to get the specialty difficulty decrease for...speeding up? Traveling through time? Freezing time? What? Such things require completely different approaches, style- and paradigm-wise. It does not make sense to have specialized foci having to encompass whole Spheres.<br /> <br /> * Sphere specialties<br /> We finally have 4+ specialty rules for spheres as well, which gives players the chance to focus the type of magick their characters do a little more. Yay for that.<br /> <br /> * Flexible Specialty Spheres per Tradition<br /> Instead of being tied to one specific specialty sphere for each Tradition, each Tradition/Convention now has a few to choose from, matching the different styles and paradigms of the various subgroups. Especially Hermes benefits from this, as some of their Houses simply are not 'Zomg Forces!'<br /> <br /> * Lots of Metaplot options<br /> M20 openly gives the ST several options wether to go hardcore dark Reckoning squash-ze-Mages metaplot or not, Avatar Storm, Technocratic control, Horizon realms - the setting per se can be as Antagonistic or relaxed as you are in the mood for.<br /> <br /> * Belief / Practice / Tools<br /> The whole sections about explaining and describing the various beliefs, practices and tools helps players to translate the character idea they have in their head into the Magick system in a much more flexible way than before. They could before of course, but this time around the corebook actively aids in that idea. One of the best changes in this edition, especially for new players.<br /> <br /> * Wonder creation<br /> Much more streamlined and simplified in the corebook, even if some examples are screwy.<br /> This makes it, IMO, much simpler for players to create the kind of Wonder they want.<br /> <br /> * Clarification of Coicidental vs. Vulgar, keeping things simple<br /> HOO vs HAB gets explained, and the book heavily weights towards 'Average Bystander' and process-driven sphere usage, keeping things simple and flexible - no Reality constantly peeking inside your pockets. HDYDT sadly breaks the process-driven part in some rulings, but see below.<br /> <br /> * Life Sphere got fixed.<br /> The Life sphere is more consistent, and finally gives you the full range of possibilities at 5 that it should have had in Revised. No more Archsphere required to turn people into frogs.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Neutral:<br /> * Paradox is back to accumulating instead of near-instantly backlashing at 5+<br /> I really consider this a near-neutral change as the nastyness of this depends on your viewpoint: Constantly getting hit with smaller Paradox backlashes that still can ruin your plans hard depending on what situation you are in like in Revised, vs. slowly building up to larger ones but being able to pull off several small effects without getting negative repercussions immediately.<br /> Bonus: The Revised rule is described and an option for those STs that want it.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Now, not all is rainbows and roses of course.<br /> The Bad:<br /> <br /> * The crossover rules in the book suck oh so damn hard for doing a pure Mage-theme game, as they don't really match the theme and fluff of the nature of how True Magick works outside the boundaries of reality, vs. the rest of the splats working within those boundaries.<br /> Fine for an even crossover-game or online games, where non-Mage players are a big consideration - but not so much for a pure Mage game, especially fluff-wise. I personally prefer keeping splat-vs-splat as pure effect-vs-effect counterspelling. But I've ranted enough about that before..<br /> <br /> * HDYDT fires a whole barrage of rule inconsistencies and arbitrary rulings at you, that simply don't match or even contradict the more elegant corebook rules. It highly overcomplicates Magick for players at times.<br /> Best treated as 'Phil's book of houserules'. Cherrypick with your players what you want and what you want to discard.<br /> To give credit where credit is due, the book itself actually tells you to do that in its first pages!<br /> <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> <br /> So there you have it, at least from my perspective. '100 times more antagonistic to the players' looks different to me.<br /> Maybe I missed something that especially grinds your gears, but on average I'd say that the book makes playing your average not-off-their-hubris-rocker Mage more relaxed and fun than Revised ever did, while still allowing a Mage to screw themselves over hard if they overdo it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 02-13-2017, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T07:48:30-08:00","id":1048239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Stuff...</div> </div> </div> </div>My toughts exactly.<br /> <br /> I also find that the description of the Spheres it's much less rich than in Revised, and far too simplified, and that's bad, you shouldn't need aditional books to figure out the Spheres. While this isn't bad for the novice who wants to start the game and doesn't understand much about Dynamic Magick, it's bad for the Mage player that want's to think deeper about the full potentiall of the Spheres.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * The system of Arete rolls has reverted to 1st/2nd/Sorc Crusade.<br /> As in, the *total* amount of successes determines the effect's parameters, instead of having to split up the dice between all of them (with the exception of Damage vs duration). The split successes rule is optional for those that want it, which is a plus.<br /> This especially allows younger Mages with smaller dice pools to achieve average effects with less rolls. No more repeated-orgies-of-ritual-rolls-for-small-things like in Revised. Thank deity-of-choice for that. Seriously. </div> </div> </div>Amen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-13-2017, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T08:01:46-08:00","id":1048245,"title":"","content":"Personally, I prefer the Revised version of Mage, the game mechanics were fairly good at encouraging players to be subtle with their use of magic. It meant that vulgar magic was reserved for emergencies and, for the most part, players used conventional methods whenever possible (though they might have used magic to augment their conventional methods). With 2nd edition rules though, things tended to get silly.<br /> <br /> For example, Mages with Correspondence 3 were rarely unarmed because they could use their magic to summon any weapon that they possessed so, if they needed their custom Desert Eagle with silver ammo, they could summon it without much difficulty (and, unlike summoning a lightning bolt, their pistol summoning might be coincidental). When compared with Mages who depended on magical direct damage, the Mage with Correspondence ended up acquiring a lot less Paradox (which is why my players tended to depend on the Mage with Correspondence 3 to be their walking arsenal). Revised discouraged blatant magic, which was a good thing in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T08:31:17-08:00","id":1048256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1048239#post1048239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My toughts exactly.<br /> <br /> I also find that the description of the Spheres it's much less rich than in Revised, and far too simplified, and that's bad, you shouldn't need aditional books to figure out the Spheres. While this isn't bad for the novice who wants to start the game and doesn't understand much about Dynamic Magick, it's bad for the Mage player that want's to think deeper about the full potentiall of the Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The sphere section of M20 leaves a lot to be desired. What's especially annoying is that there are subtle changes between Revised and M20 (prime aura reading, Forces damage, Spirit providing soak for Sprit Rage) some of which are only stated, others are only mentioned in completely different sections of the book. There are not many rotes to help illustrate the difference in levels, and many of the common magical effects just leave you to hunt around for the mechanics.<br /> I get the impression they expect us to assume it's the same as Revised unless stated, which makes it difficult to judge in case the rule is around but obscured.<br /> <br /> Oh, and can we briefly mention the god awful formatting? Revised wasn't much better, but at least they understood the concept of Section Breaks, and would clutter the page with space destroying images quite as much. The sphere section of M20 requires a lot of attention just to follow.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm in two minds about effect parameters not being built into. I kinda like you have to decide which successes go into area, damage, duration, and effect. It makes building big effects feel more substantial.<br /> I get that it makes almost everything require a ritual to work, but I get around that by having up to the first 10 successes not increase difficulty per roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T09:28:14-08:00","id":1048278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1046271#post1046271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Use Alchemy 6, you can become a Revenant and Quarter the rate again forever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You could also just, you know... make a potion of true immortality at that level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T10:20:06-08:00","id":1048303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1048278#post1048278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You could also just, you know... make a potion of true immortality at that level.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be a much more costly process at my table. And it would need replenishing... Short of truly legendary tools and ingredients.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T16:25:29-08:00","id":1048466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1046066-immortality?p=1048303#post1048303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be a much more costly process at my table. And it would need replenishing... Short of truly legendary tools and ingredients.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the point we're talking about level 6 paths(the point just after 5 dots when paths start to meet or exceed diciplines and gifts in level of power at equal rank), your sorcerer would feesably already have legendary tools and ingredients or at least the means to aquire them(not that they'd be easy to aquire, just it's doable). <br /> <br /> Though becoming a revenant has it's own benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T05:13:58-08:00","id":1048679,"title":"","content":"Even just in the core book they make magic excessively complicated.<br /> <br /> You are a wizard and you want to summon a taxi, literally? Good luck with your engineering rolls to actually design a taxi from scratch. Every single time.<br /> <br /> You want to do a thing? Every possible sphere it so much as looks at must be included.<br /> <br /> Not to mention the whole paragraph about how you should consider doing things with your mundane resources a spell you should roll Arete for.<br /> <br /> If they hadn't stopped splitting the dice pool the game would be unplayable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 02-14-2017, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}